/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store

# cargo-packager installer output (bundles are built in CI, never committed)
/dist/
**/target/

# editor
/.idea
/.vscode
*.swp
*.swo

# personal notes (not part of the project)
/.personal/

# generated review decks / working notes — keep the Typst source, not the PDF
/docs/reviews/*.pdf
/docs/notes/*.pdf

# mdbook build output — rebuilt by `just docs`, published from CI
/docs/book/

# The single-instance lock, when a run lands it in the working directory
# instead of the temp dir — which is what an *empty* (not unset) TMPDIR
# produces, since `std::env::temp_dir()` then yields a relative path.
dev.termherd.lock

# cargo-mutants scratch output (mutation testing runs locally / in CI)
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# Claude Code local (per-machine) settings — never shared. The shared
# .claude/settings.json may be tracked; the *.local.json overlay is not.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Local git worktrees (per-machine working copies); never repo content.
.claude/worktrees/
# Local PRDs, planning notes, and extracted artifacts; locally controlled.
.local/
# Per-directory tool caches the impeccable skill drops beside the sources it
# reads; they reappear on every run, so ignore rather than clean repeatedly.
.impeccable/
